Also, `application/array+json` on "hello\n" → "unable to unmarshal array hello\n: yaml: unmarshal errors:..." → so JSONArray = the array parse with the "unable to unmarshal array" prefix ✓.

And what about `application/array+json` with a map input? Let me test: `-d d=person.json?type=application/array+json`.

Also for `application/yaml` with an array input "[1,2]" → should give [1 2] ✓.

And empty input with type=application/json → map[] (empty map!). Interesting: for empty data, JSON → map[] (so the object unmarshal of "" succeeded?!). Hmm, `yaml.Unmarshal([]byte(""), &m)` → succeeds with an empty map ✓ (yaml of empty input is a nil document → unmarshal into map gives empty map? Actually yaml.Unmarshal of "" into a map pointer → leaves the map as-is (empty) ✓).

And for `application/yaml` with empty data → ? Let me test.

Let me test these edge cases. Also the text/plain type returns the raw string.

Let me also check: what happens with an unknown mime → "data of type \"bogus/x\" not yet supported" ✓.

Let me test a few more.

